    {
      "id": "claim_a4fe79f418564f6ca70300aaab477bd5",
      "statement": "SkeletonAnimation memoizes clip validation on a composite key of clip, Skeleton.ContentHash and the live DFS bone count, because reading curve bindings walks every curve in the clip (730 for a walk cycle) on every inspector repaint, and because ClearRuntimeCaches is not triggered by a rig reimport.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Animation/SkeletonAnimation.cs#L117-L144",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d016416ba64dbcb4fe1b67bcfd9a9a2a82ce2b9a6b59e762b7c0571b6af2a5e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_21455882055f4d2e9958ed46e6b139cc",
      "statement": "The live bone count is part of the validation cache key specifically because Skeleton.ContentHash is derived from the skeleton's own cached bone list and so cannot change in the one case the check most needs to catch: a rig whose bones changed underneath a skeleton that has not noticed yet.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Animation/SkeletonAnimation.cs#L117-L144",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d016416ba64dbcb4fe1b67bcfd9a9a2a82ce2b9a6b59e762b7c0571b6af2a5e:"
        }
